@page "/docs/dialog-service"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.DialogService
<PageTitle>Dialog Service - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Dialog Service</h1>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">imperative</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">awaitable results</BzBadge>
        </div>
        <p>Open dialogs imperatively from C# - confirmations, prompts, or any component - and <code>await</code> the result, instead of wiring markup and open state by hand. Built on the same Dialog, AlertDialog and Sheet components, so focus, scroll-lock, and animations behave identically.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock SetupSnippet="DialogService/UsageSetup" Snippet="DialogService/Usage"
                Description="Register the service and host once, then inject IDialogService and await a dialog from C# - no markup or open state to wire by hand." />

    @* Setup and API are reference, not examples: plain code sections (no preview frame to leave
       empty) and h2s, so the TOC lists them beside Usage instead of nesting them under Examples. *@
    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Setup</h2>
        <p>Register the service once and drop a single host at your app root.</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="DialogService/Setup" />
        <p>Already wired up in this docs app (<code>AddBlaizio()</code> in <code>Program.cs</code> and one <code>&lt;DialogProvider /&gt;</code> in the layout), so every demo below is live.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">API</h2>
        <p>Inject <code>IDialogService</code> anywhere and call one of:</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="DialogService/IDialogService" />
    </section>

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Confirmation" Description="The common case: a yes/no question that resolves to a bool."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceConfirmExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Destructive, custom labels" Description="Override the button text and variant via BzDialogOptions."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceDestructiveExample)" />

    <Demo Title="A component as the dialog" Description="Show any component with ShowAsync<T>; it closes itself with a typed value."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceComponentExample)" />

    <Demo Title="An inline template" Description="Pass a RenderFragment straight to ShowAsync; the template receives the instance."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceTemplateExample)" />

    <Demo Title="A sheet instead of a window" Description="ShowSheetAsync shows the same content in the Sheet skin, sliding from the edge you pick (Start/End are logical and mirror under RTL). Component and template overloads both exist; the result flow is unchanged."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceSheetExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Stacking" Description="A confirm fired from inside an open dialog layers on top - focus trapping and scroll-lock nest correctly, and the page stays locked until the last one closes."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceStackedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Locked while busy" Description="A component sets Dialog.PreventDismiss while a lengthy op runs, so Escape, the backdrop, and the close button can't dismiss it until it finishes - then it closes itself."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceBusyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization" Description="An inline template gives you the whole dialog body - here a branded upgrade prompt with a coloured icon header and a custom primary button - while the service still handles focus, scroll-lock and the result."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceCustomizationExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Service dialogs follow the app's direction; a dialog body can also opt into RTL itself with a DirectionProvider. Here the header, text and footer buttons mirror with Arabic or Hebrew copy."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceRtlExample)" />

</div>

